  "faqs": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)",
  "@faqs": {
    "description": "Help dialog FAQ header"
  },
  "helpQ1": "Why isn't FillUp calculating my mileage?",
  "@helpQ1": {
    "description": "FAQ question 1"
  },
  "helpA1": "You need to fill your tank once to establish a starting point, and then continue recording all of your fuel purchases. Each time you fill your tank after the starting point, FillUp will calculate your mileage by determining the distance driven and fuel used since the previous full tank.\n\nTIP: In the Add Fuel screen, put a check mark in the \"Tank Full\" box to indicate when the tank has been filled, otherwise FillUp will never calculate mileage.",
  "@helpA1": {
    "description": "FAQ answer 1"
  },
  "helpQ2": "Why does FillUp only estimate my mileage?",
  "@helpQ2": {
    "description": "FAQ question 2"
  },
  "helpA2": "A full tank is needed to accurately calculate how much fuel was used since the previous full tank. When you get fuel and the tank is not full, FillUp cannot calculate mileage exactly. Instead it will allow you to estimate mileage.",
  "@helpA2": {
    "description": "FAQ answer 2"
  },
  "helpQ3": "What if I forget to record a fuel purchase?",
  "@helpQ3": {
    "description": "FAQ question 3"
  },
  "helpA3": "The next time you fill your tank, the mileage calculation will be wrong (too high). You can hide this value by selecting it in the Log and clicking \"Hide Calculation\".",
  "@helpA3": {
    "description": "FAQ answer 3"
  },
  "helpQ4": "How do I backup/restore my data?",
  "@helpQ4": {
    "description": "FAQ question 4"
  },
  "helpA4": "FillUp Log data is stored in a database on your device. Use Export to save Log data to a CSV file, and Import to restore it.",
  "@helpA4": {
    "description": "FAQ answer 4"
  },
